.TH FZD 1 "FZD" "FZD" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fzd \- fast keyboard-driven terminal file explorer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fzd_cd
.br
.B lf
.RI [ keywords ...| directory ]
.br
.B lff
.RI [ query ...]
.br
.B fzd
.SH DESCRIPTION
FZD browses the current directory with fzf, previews files and directories,
and supports global search and safe single-item file operations.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
Add this line to your Bash or zsh startup file, then open a new shell:
.PP
.nf
\&. /usr/share/fzd/integration.sh
.fi
.PP
Run fzd_cd, or lf if that name was free when integration was sourced.
Selecting a directory changes the calling shell's directory.
With keywords, lf jumps directly using upstream zoxide, falling back to global
discovery when no match exists. Existing directory arguments change directory
directly. lff always opens global discovery, optionally with a seeded query;
fzd_find is the alternative when lff is already in use.
Raw fzd prints the selected directory instead.
Installation never changes users' startup files or configuration.
.PP
Zoxide is required. Explorer visits are learned on exit. In interactive shells,
FZD initializes upstream zoxide learning only when not already initialized;
existing z/zi commands and hook preferences are preserved. Native Tab completion
uses learned directories. Inline suggestions require a user-installed engine;
zsh-autosuggestions needs its completion strategy to suggest learned names.
.SH CONTROLS
Left/Right navigate parent/child directories. Enter selects a directory or
opens a file in the editor. Esc cancels. Type to fuzzy filter; Ctrl+F opens
global search. Alt+Left/Right traverse history; Alt+H shows recent directories.
.PP
Ctrl+C/X/V copy/cut/paste; Alt+C/X/V are alternatives. Ctrl+R or F2 renames.
Ctrl+N or F7 creates a directory. F8 requests confirmed, recoverable Trash.
F1 shows contextual help. Ctrl+G exits. Delete edits the query.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Defaults work without a configuration file. Optional trusted Bash settings
are read from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fzd/fzd.conf, defaulting to ~/.config/fzd/fzd.conf.
FZD_CONF_FILE selects another path. An example is installed at
/usr/share/fzd/fzd.conf.example.
.PP
EDITOR or VISUAL selects a single executable, without arguments; micro is the
fallback. FZD_BIN selects an alternate executable for shell integration.
.SH STATE
Recent directories and the internal clipboard live below
${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/fzd/explorer/.
Removing the package preserves user configuration and state.
.SH TRASH
F8 requires gio (libglib2.0-bin on Debian/Ubuntu, glib2 on Arch/Fedora) or
trash-put (trash-cli). Permanent deletion is never substituted.
Restore through your desktop's Trash or the installed Trash tool.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/doc/fzd/TECHNICAL.md (possibly compressed) documents controls,
configuration, unusual filenames and terminal shortcut limitations.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at https://github.com/seanap/fzd/issues.
